739	    <!-- ── Link Button ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
740	    <section class="section">
741	      <h2 class="section-title">Link-style Button (for low-emphasis actions)</h2>
742	      <p class="section-desc">A <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> that renders as an inline text link. For low-emphasis inline actions that don't warrant a boxed button shape. Uses Library Grey (<code>--grey</code>) — subtly distinct from body text and clearly readable on both white (5.8:1) and Warm Wash (5.5:1). The underline is sufficient affordance in UI contexts. Hover shifts the underline to lime, signalling interactivity with the brand accent without changing text colour.</p>
743	
744	      <table class="states-table">
745	        <thead>
746	          <tr>
747	            <th scope="col" style="text-align:left; width:110px;">State</th>
748	            <th scope="col" colspan="5" style="text-align:left;">Example</th>
749	          </tr>
750	        </thead>
751	        <tbody>
752	          <tr>
753	            <td>Default</td>
754	            <td colspan="5" style="text-align:left; padding-left:24px;">
755	              <button class="btn-link">Reset to default</button>
756	            </td>
757	          </tr>
758	          <tr>
759	            <td>Hover</td>
760	            <td colspan="5" style="text-align:left; padding-left:24px;">
761	              <button class="btn-link sim-hover">Reset to default</button>
762	            </td>
763	          </tr>
764	          <tr>
765	            <td>Focus</td>
766	            <td colspan="5" style="text-align:left; padding-left:24px;">
767	              <button class="btn-link sim-focus">Reset to default</button>
768	            </td>
769	          </tr>
770	          <tr>
771	            <td>Disabled</td>
772	            <td colspan="5" style="text-align:left; padding-left:24px;">
773	              <button class="btn-link sim-disabled" disabled>Reset to default</button>
774	            </td>
775	          </tr>
776	        </tbody>
777	      </table>
778	
779	      <h3 style="font-size:14px; font-weight:700; margin: 28px 0 12px;">In Context</h3>
780	
781	      <div class="context-row">
782	        <span class="context-label">Inline in UI text</span>
783	        <p style="margin:0; font-size:14px; line-height:1.7; max-width:560px;">
784	          Showing 5 of 1,317 sessions.
785	          <button class="btn-link">View all sessions</button>
786	        </p>
787	        <p style="margin:0; font-size:14px; line-height:1.7; max-width:560px;">
788	          3 categories selected.
789	          <button class="btn-link">Clear selection</button>
790	          &nbsp;·&nbsp;
791	          <button class="btn-link">Select all</button>
792	        </p>
793	      </div>
794	
795	      <div class="context-row" style="margin-top:12px;">
796	        <span class="context-label">Alongside a form field</span>
797	        <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:6px; font-size:14px;">
798	          <label style="font-weight:600; color:#6b6459;">Username</label>
799	          <div style="display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px;">
800	            <input type="text" value="brath" style="padding:7px 10px; border:1px solid #d4cfc9; border-radius:4px; font-size:14px; font-family:inherit;" readonly>
801	            <button class="btn-link">Change username</button>
802	          </div>
803	        </div>
804	      </div>
805	
806	      <p class="callout" style="margin-top:16px;">
807	        <strong>Colour decision:</strong> <code>.btn-link</code> uses Library Grey (<code>#6b6459</code>), not blue and not the near-black body text. The slightly lighter tone gives the button a subtle distinction from surrounding copy — useful when scanning a dense page — while staying entirely within the neutral palette. No blue needed: the underline communicates interactivity in UI contexts. AA on white (5.8:1) and Warm Wash (5.5:1).
808	      </p>
809	      <p class="callout">
810	        <strong>Content hyperlinks (<code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tags):</strong> Use <code>--link: #1f5e96</code> (Archival Blue, 6.8:1 on white — AA ✓). The brand's designated Link Blue (<code>#1e8bc3</code>) is only 3.8:1 and fails AA. Note: Archival Blue contrasts with Repository Brown body text at only 2.6:1, below the 3:1 threshold for colour-alone differentiability (WCAG 1.4.1) — <strong><code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tags must always be underlined</strong> to satisfy the standard.
811	      </p>
812	      <p class="callout">
813	        <strong>When to use vs. a tertiary button:</strong> Use a link-style button when the action is <em>inline within content or a label</em>, or when adding a box would create visual clutter in a dense layout. Use a tertiary button when the action is part of an <em>explicit action group</em> (e.g. alongside Save and Cancel).
814	      </p>
815	    </section>
